WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.942
By the end of this module, you should be able to build a cleaning workflow rather than a

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:06.322
one-off fix.

00:00:06.322 --> 00:00:14.462
You should be able to profile quality problems, normalize representation, validate rules, identify duplicates,

00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:17.647
and use safer SQL patterns for changes.

00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:23.467
You should also be able to explain what your cleaning logic knows and what it does not know.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:28.467
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:32.667
a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:39.842
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:41.817
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:48.707
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:52.377
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:56.622
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
